    "formula": "P(J_h2@1 | do(W@1=w)) = sum_z P(J_h2@1 | W@1=w, z) P(z) over z in each minimal set",
    "reading": "Back-door paths leave W@t through its parents I@t, Ev@t, W@(t-1) and W_max (phi). S opens W <- Ev <- S -> T -> k -> J, W <- I <- S -> T -> k -> J and, through the previous slice, W(t) <- Ev(t) <- S -> I(t-1) -> N(t-1) -> N(t) -> psi_o -> psi -> A -> k -> J. Adjusting for T@t alone leaves the last route open; I@(t-1), I@t and W@(t-1) are also needed (W <- I -> N and W(t-1) -> N(t-1) -> N(t)). The search finds two minimal sets: one contains T@t, the other replaces T@t by Ev@(t-1), Ev@t. Temperature is therefore a sufficient blocker, not a necessary one: without T the effect is still identified through the evaporation record, and it is lost by back-door only if both T and Ev are unmeasured (or phi is).",
    "positivity_caveat": "Identification here is graphical. The Sonoran campaigns have near-collinear moisture and temperature across seasons, so the strata of the adjustment set are almost empty at the contrasts of interest (a positivity violation); that, not the graph, is why the Q10 question was not resolved.",
    "limits": "back-door only: no front-door or full ID-algorithm; absence of a set is not a proof of non-identifiability",
    "verdict": "identified by back-door given phi, I@(t-1), I@t, W@(t-1) and either T@t or Ev@(t-1), Ev@t; no back-door set otherwise"
  }
